 "text": "Hey there, how are you holding up? Clean them with brush across the bristles, not down, and never dip them. If they' really bad, pick out the worst with small brush hog, then use very hand full of brush tube. That's too long. A few hours maximum, or dry them thoroughly before going to bed. You can often improve them by soaking them in warm water with a drop of dish soap, then gently working it with another brush. Dry them very well after. Then get fresh brushes regularly and keep an eye on them. Some brushes are just meant be replaced every year or two.",
